# Configure clients; do not hardcode them

Canonical: `docs/GOTIGIN_CONFIGURE_NOT_HARDCODE.md`. Kumkaj detail:
`kumkaj-workspace/docs/CLIENT_TEMPLATES_AND_SETUP.md` (when that tree is
available).

## Fact

Gotigin brand apps (Kumkaj and others) implement features **for** many
client setups. The product stays one app for that trade; **templates,
Settings, and rights** show or hide chrome so each shop sees what it
needs (e.g. hide kitchen communication when counter and kitchen are
adjacent). Agents often forget this and push toward a one-client
concrete face.

## Do

- Prefer configuration, defaults, and progressive depth over forking or
  deleting capability.
- Keep Wadhu crates brand-neutral and optional; never bake a restaurant
  or courier client layout into a generic crate.

## Do not

- Treat a single client’s request as permanent hardcoding of the only
  product face.
- Put brand client packs / shop business logic into Wadhu
  (`independent-parts.mdc`, vision §4).
